  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates whether a lottery contains a sure outcome (i.e., a 100% probability of a specific monetary amount). In this decision problem, Lottery A offers a sure outcome of 2400 Euros with 100% probability, while Lottery B does not have a sure outcome—its outcomes are 2500 Euros (33%), 2400 Euros (66%), and 0 Euros (1%). Therefore, the decision reason can be applied: it prefers the lottery without a sure outcome, which would be Lottery B. The relevant information (presence of sure outcome) is clearly derivable from the lotteries' structure.",
